{0 KV}

Store and list text values by key with {!Workero.KV}, the supported subset of
{{:https://developers.cloudflare.com/kv/}Workers KV}. KV is eventually
consistent across locations. Changes often become visible elsewhere within
60 seconds, but 60 seconds is not a guaranteed upper bound.

{1 Configure the binding}

For local development, put this in [wrangler.toml]. Wrangler creates local
storage when you run [opam exec -- wrangler dev]:

{@toml[
[[kv_namespaces]]
binding = "KV"
]}

{1 Write the Worker}

{@ocaml[
let handler req env _ctx =
  let open Workero in
  let kv = KV.of_env env "KV" in
  let url = Request.url req in
  let key = Option.value (URL.query url "k") ~default:"" in
  match (Request.method_ req, URL.path url) with
  | GET, "/kv" -> (
      match KV.get kv key with
      | Some value -> Response.text value
      | None -> Response.text ~status:`Not_Found "not found\n")
  | PUT, "/kv" ->
      KV.put ~expiration_ttl:3600 kv key (Request.text req);
      Response.text "stored\n"
  | DELETE, "/kv" ->
      KV.delete kv key;
      Response.text "deleted\n"
  | GET, "/keys" ->
      let prefix = URL.query url "prefix" in
      Response.text (String.concat "\n" (KV.list ?prefix kv) ^ "\n")
  | _ -> Response.text ~status:`Not_Found "not found\n"

let () = Workero.serve handler
]}

[KV.get] returns [None] for a missing key. [KV.put] takes text and an optional
expiration time in seconds (at least 60). [KV.delete] accepts a missing key.
[KV.list] returns names in lexicographic order. It follows cursors across pages
of at most 1000 keys and holds all names in memory. It raises [Failure] if KV
reports an incomplete page without a cursor. See {!Workero.KV} for the API.

{1 Verify locally}

Run [opam exec -- wrangler dev] in one terminal. In a second terminal:

{@sh[
curl -X PUT -d hello "http://localhost:8787/kv?k=greeting"
curl "http://localhost:8787/kv?k=greeting"
curl "http://localhost:8787/keys?prefix=greet"
]}

The responses are [stored], [hello] and [greeting], in that order.

{1 Deploy with an existing namespace}

Remote creation requires an authenticated Wrangler. If you do not let
{{:https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/wrangler/configuration/#automatic-provisioning}Wrangler provision it on deploy},
create a namespace and copy its printed ID into [wrangler.toml]:

{@sh[
opam exec -- wrangler kv namespace create KV
]}

{@toml[
[[kv_namespaces]]
binding = "KV"
id = "<namespace id>"
]}

See {{:https://developers.cloudflare.com/kv/get-started/}Cloudflare KV setup}
and {{:https://developers.cloudflare.com/kv/api/list-keys/}listing keys}.
See {{!page-getting_started}Getting started} for deployment steps.
